// A clustered index's archetype, its rows moved into the index's order on
// the CPU, read by a `gpu` system: the columns it moved go to the GPU
// (where its update ran, as its condition was before it: the update
// makes the index up to date).
// RUN: sed -e 's/^system walk() {/gpu system walk() {/' %S/Inputs/clustered.ent > %t.cl.ent
// RUN: %ent run %S/Inputs/clustered.ent > %t.cl.cpu
// RUN: %ent run %t.cl.ent --gpu > %t.cl.gpu
// RUN: diff %t.cl.cpu %t.cl.gpu

// Rows given to buffers in a `gpu` system, by a `for ... by` and by a
// plain `for`, read by the next `for` of the same system: the GPU's copy
